e while they're in the sensory  deprivation like all the time like when  they get brought out of it like all of  their senses kind of like are are  heightened you know what i mean so  whenever the staff at the facility or  the higher-ups rather like when they get  asked to  like we need some information about this  terrorist attack or this head of a drug  cartel or this arms dealer or whatever  the hell  then the staff will pick one of the  antennas and they will do something  called tuning them  which basically entails turning off the  nerve gas that they keep them on all the  time and it kind of causes all of their  senses to like rush back in in this  state they actually like are getting  like all these flows of information and  they found that like all this  information is actually really good like  actionable intelligence because they're  getting stuff like from the ether  now the sad thing about this though i  mean like i said it is very effective  they can give all this you know  information that is proven to be correct  about whatever target that they're  that they've chose to like tune into it  also causes the antennas themselves  horrible excruciating pain and really  like unbearable mental anguish like i  said he he describes it like joe  describes it at one point it's like hey  you know like when you know you fall  asleep on your arm and like your arms  asleep and then you wake it up and it's  like and it's really really painful like  as the sensation comes back into it he's  like it's like that but like a million  times worse like because they can't feel  their bodies and they can't see but then  everything comes like rushing back to  them at once when they take them off the  nerve gas and it's like really  horrifying for them now over time the  staff of the facility have kind of had  to train themselves to see the antennas  as pieces of equipment rather than human  beings  nobody in the facility uh knows where  the antennas came from or who they were  